<title>UK: Russia's Black Sea port of Novorossiisk reopens.</title>
<headline>Russia's Black Sea port of Novorossiisk reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea reopened early on Wednesday after a 15-hour closure caused by bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port closed at 1600 local time on Tuesday because of high winds and swell but reopened again at 0700 on Wednesday, the source added.</p>
<p>Two crude tankers were alongside, with another one at anchor outside the port.</p>
<p>Tuapse, also on the Black Sea, remained shut on Wednesday after closing at 1300 local time on Tuesday because of bad weather, but Odessa and the Baltic port of Ventspils were operating normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
